    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3485" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος</span>) 
			Ep.
		Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hill-top,
				mountain peak</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, always in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκριες
			ἠνεμόεσσαι</span> windy <i>mountain tops</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.400
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				382
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἄκριας</span> through
				<i>hill-country</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.281
			</span></i>:— sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περγαμίης ὑπὲρ ἄκριος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					1035.8
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam.).</div>
